"reasons": [
{"id":"file-not-run:native-burst","measured":"file-not-run","kind":"environment","missing":"The simulation replaces the native DPDK burst path with its in-memory link, so no run transmits or receives through a device queue pair, where a link that is down, a poisoned or unverified registration, a receive pool other than the queue's, an unsendable first datagram or a device that prepares none of the chains refuses the burst; the register counts only construction sites of the crate's non-test build, so both rows read as not reached although the in-memory link (`crates/kestrike/src/net/link.rs`, compiled under `cfg(test)`) returned `Failed` from `LinkEnd::call_fault` 3,668 times in the run at `9ca0dee8563c` (roots 1 to 50) and returns `Closed` from a closed end.","sentence":""},
{"id":"file-not-run:activation-envelope","measured":"file-not-run","kind":"unconstructible","missing":"No profile builds an owner's activation envelope and checks it against the owner's declared memory, and no code of the workspace's non-test build calls `Envelope::new`, `check`, `total` or `covered_by` either; only the module's tests and Kani proofs do.","sentence":""},
{"id":"function-not-entered:endpoint-config","measured":"function-not-entered","functions":[["net/memory.rs","EndpointConfig::validate"]],"kind":"unconstructible","missing":"No profile validates an endpoint configuration against an arena, and no code of the workspace's non-test build calls `EndpointConfig::validate` either; only tests (`net/memory_tests.rs`, `native/env_tests.rs`, `native/burst_tests.rs`) present zero peers, a request-slot or peer-share shape out of range, an arena without both packet kinds, a short receive data room, a batch of zero or above the receive reserve, a reserve at or above the pool's count, or a slot and peer count whose request-table charge overflows.","sentence":""},
{"id":"function-not-entered:changed-frame-body","measured":"function-not-entered","functions":[["net/frame.rs","bad"],["net/ownership.rs","OwnershipBody::encode"],["net/ownership.rs","OwnershipBody::ordered"],["net/ownership.rs","ReadyBody::ordered"],["net/ownership.rs","identity"]],"kind":"fault","missing":"No profile changes a datagram's bytes in flight: the frame parse (`check_kind`) checks each kind's header fields and body before the header crc and the tag, so a changed byte in a checked header field (the link's `Header` class on a HELLO's epoch, for one), a READY body whose shard is zero, or a READY body of another length under a matching datagram length would fail them, and no profile arms the link's `Effect::Corrupt` rule; an ownership envelope with a zero shard or a bad length (`OwnershipBody::ordered`) would also need an ownership query, which no profile sends, and the encoder-side sites, the frame encoder's own pass over the same checks (`ordered`, from `admitted` and `fold_ordered`, for a GET with a zero grant, say), `carried` for a bootstrap or ownership body sent in more than one slice and `OwnershipBody::encode` for an output buffer of another length, refuse only arguments the crate's non-test senders never pass.","sentence":""},
{"id":"function-not-entered:ownership-query","measured":"function-not-entered","functions":[["net/ownership.rs","OwnershipBody::encode"],["net/ownership.rs","OwnershipBody::ordered"],["net/ownership.rs","Validity::new"]],"kind":"step","missing":"No profile sends a WHO-HOLDS or PROBE ownership query, and no code of the crate's non-test build sends one either, so no ownership envelope crosses the link; an envelope's ordered checks (`OwnershipBody::ordered`) refuse it as `Volume`, `Flags`, `ReportAge`, `Responder` or `Reserved` only for a malformed volume, validity, report-age, responder or reserved field, which would also need a changed byte in flight, and the encoder-side sites refuse only a body the crate's non-test senders never build: `Validity::new` rejects a validity bit outside the three defined, and `OwnershipBody::encode` rejects a noncanonical volume name, any validity bit on a query, a Report bit without a volume, a Serving or Live bit without a tenure, a report age without the Report bit, or a responder on a query or none on a reply.","sentence":""},
{"id":"function-not-entered:ownership-kind","measured":"function-not-entered","functions":[["net/ownership.rs","OwnershipBody::encode"],["net/ownership.rs","OwnershipBody::ordered"]],"kind":"unconstructible","missing":"No code of the workspace's non-test build encodes or decodes an ownership body under a frame kind outside the six ownership kinds through the public `OwnershipBody::encode` or `OwnershipBody::decode`: the crate's code passes only the six ownership kinds to `OwnershipBody::ordered` (the parse's match arm and the owner's and client's ownership arms) and only HOLDER or WRONG-OWNER to `OwnershipBody::encode`.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:changed-datagram","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"fault","missing":"No profile changes a datagram's bytes in flight: no profile arms the link's `Effect::Corrupt` rule, whose classes flip the last header byte the crc covers, the tag's first byte or the first body byte, the magic, header-length, version, kind, flag, reserved and datagram-length checks would need a change at their own offsets, and a READY body's caps (whose first byte the body classes flip) or tenure a change in that body; the encoder-side sites (the frame encoder's own `ordered` pass, which runs `ReadyBody::decode` on the sender's READY body, `carried` for a declared length other than the payload's, `ReadyBody::encode` for caps out of range or an invalid tenure) refuse only arguments the crate's non-test senders never pass, and `Owner::take_question` decodes again a WHO-HOLDS or PROBE body the parse already accepted, so its `Malformed` would also need a query, which no profile sends.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:keyed-peer-frame","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"fault","missing":"No profile has a peer that holds the session key send a frame the crate's own encoders never produce: a PUT DATA or GET DATA frame whose body crc field differs from its body (a body byte changed in flight fails the tag first), or a request at wire generation `GENERATION_LIMIT`, one above the last generation the crate's client draws.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:stranger-datagram","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"step","missing":"No profile attaches a stranger link to the owner's simulated transport (`Mux::with_stranger`) or relabels a datagram as a stranger's, the only ways a datagram reaches the owner with no peer; the native wire refuses an unknown source before the owner sees it.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:peer-principal","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"configuration","missing":"No profile configures a peer to send under a principal other than the one the owner's key ring assigns to that peer.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:key-set","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"configuration","missing":"No profile loads or replaces a key ring or PUT permit set with a key of the wrong length, an entry or permit for an unconfigured principal, a principal named twice, a configured peer without a key, two principals sharing one key, a replacement at the ring's own epoch or more than 65,535 peers, or starts a client or an owner whose remaining engine budget is below its key ring's or its PUT permits' charge, a `KeyError::Budget` that `ClientError::Keys`, `OwnerError::Keys` and `OwnerError::Permits` carry.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:engine-budget","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"configuration","missing":"No profile starts a client or an owner with an engine budget smaller than the charge of its key ring, PUT permits, sessions, scratch, request tables, client namespace, fetch, upload, serve or PUT core, or takes source slots (`memory::sources`) under a budget smaller than their charge.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:entropy","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"fault","missing":"No profile makes the entropy source that draws a session nonce fail or return an all-zero nonce, at a client's start, an owner's start or an owner's rekey.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:client-start","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"configuration","missing":"No profile starts a client with a batch of zero, a slot cap or window cap outside its bounds, a receive pool whose data cap is below the fetch boxes, whose control reserve is below the receive ring plus the batch or whose data room is below one datagram, fewer fetch boxes than the fetch window, a release board smaller than the request table's slots or already attached, more than 65,536 source slots, or a remaining engine budget below the charge of its request namespace, fetch core or upload core, a `FetchCoreError::Budget` that `ClientError::Fetch` carries.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:owner-start","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"configuration","missing":"No profile starts an owner over parts of different storages, with a cap, request, PUT, run-waiter, fill, watermark-floor, GET-reserve, follower, batch or maintenance setting its checks refuse, with more read slots or buffers than the volume's read shape, with a read shape whose read span is below one fragment or cannot hold the header first, or while a response buffer is lent out.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:endpoint-memory","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"configuration","missing":"No profile builds a packet pool over a pool kind that is not a packet kind or has no buffers, a buffer length with no packet layout, a control reserve at or above the pool's count or a pool whose view another packet pool already claimed, or asks `memory::sources` for more source slots than the read-response pool holds or than 65,536, from a pool with buffers shorter than one fragment or with fewer free buffers than the count.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:client-request-unrouted","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"step","missing":"No profile issues a GET, PUT or INVALIDATE from a client before its owner session is active, while the client holds no route binding the owner's shard to the session's tenure or while its route is withheld, or an INVALIDATE whose low version is above its high one.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:owner-rekey","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"step","missing":"No profile rekeys an owner while one of the owner's requests is live (`RekeyError::Busy`, which `OwnerRekeyError::Rekey` also carries) or after a panic poisoned the owner (`OwnerRekeyError::Poisoned`); `OwnerRekeyError::Rekey` also carries refused replacement keys, which `not-constructed:key-set` names.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:upload-shape","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"step","missing":"No profile's client prepares or supplies an upload against its shape: a second PREPARE with another shape, a PREPARE with a TTL of zero, a fragment index outside the shape or already supplied, or a fragment of another length than the shape gives its index.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:namespace-admission","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"unconstructible","missing":"No code of the workspace's non-test build calls the public `Namespace::admit` or `Namespace::admissible` with a peer or wire slot outside the namespace, or with a generation at or below the watermark of an unbound in-range slot: the owner admits a request only after `route` returned `Fresh`, which excludes all three, and a bound slot answers `Busy` first.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:chunk-length","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"unconstructible","missing":"No profile builds a fragment geometry through the public `FragmentGeometry::new` with a record chunk length of zero or not a multiple of 4096, and no code of the workspace's non-test build does either: the owner passes only the chunk length `RecordConfig::validate` already held positive and a multiple of 4096.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:paired-core","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"unconstructible","missing":"No profile builds a second fetch core or a second upload core on one client request table through the public `FetchCore::new` or `UploadCore::new`, and no code of the workspace's non-test build does either: a client builds one fetch core and one upload core on a fresh request table.","sentence":""},
{"id":"not-constructed:short-datagram","measured":"not-constructed","kind":"fault","missing":"No profile delivers, without the link's truncation flag, a datagram shorter than a frame header: the link's truncation sets that flag, which `checked` answers with `Truncated` before it reads a byte.","sentence":""}
